    "body": "Having done this I thought another improvement might be possible, basically doing the same thing I've done here when serializing and thereby avoiding the magic placeholder objects. However\r\n```html\r\n<script>\r\nx = new ArrayBuffer(2);\r\ntry {\r\n  postMessage(Symbol(), \"*\", [x]);\r\n} catch(e) {\r\n  w(x.byteLength);\r\n}\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nlogs 2 in Live DOM Viewer. (It doesn't throw in Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=182380.)\r\n\r\nI guess we might still be able to do it, but we cannot do any destructive stuff until after StructuredSerializeInternal() has run.",
